msgid "old code only - do not use it in new code"
msgstr "само в стар код - не го използвайте в нов код"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:81
msgid "Start with `const`"
msgstr "Започвайте с `const`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:82
msgid "Write `const` by default. Change it to `let` only when you really need to give the variable a new value. Good rule guidelines ask the same for global variables: *\"they must be declared as const\"*."
msgstr "Пишете `const` по подразбиране. Сменете го с `let` само когато наистина трябва да дадете нова стойност на variable. Добрите насоки за правилата искат същото за глобалните variables: *\"they must be declared as const\"*."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:87 site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:117 site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:252 site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:359 site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:399
msgid "Animation"
msgstr "Анимация"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:88
msgid "**Variables in memory:** [5. `const`](../animations/variablesInMemory.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Variables в паметта:** [5. `const`](../animations/variablesInMemory.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:91
msgid "Strict mode: no variables by accident"
msgstr "Strict mode: без случайни variables"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:93
msgid "Without `let`, `const` or `var`, JavaScript silently creates a **global** variable. A typo in a name then creates a new variable instead of an error:"
msgstr "Без `let`, `const` или `var` JavaScript тихо създава **глобална** variable. Тогава печатна грешка в името създава нова variable, вместо да даде грешка:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:102
msgid "Put `\"use strict\";` as the **first line** of a file (or function), and the same mistake becomes an error:"
msgstr "Сложете `\"use strict\";` като **първи ред** на файла (или на функцията) и същата грешка вече спира програмата:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:113
msgid "Modules and classes are always in strict mode. In the practice files we start with `\"use strict\";`."
msgstr "Модулите и класовете винаги са в strict mode. Във файловете за упражнения започваме с `\"use strict\";`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:118
msgid "**Variable scope:** [4. No declaration and `\"use strict\"`](../animations/scopeChain.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Scope на variables:** [4. Без деклариране и `\"use strict\"`](../animations/scopeChain.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:121
msgid "2. Naming variables"
msgstr "2. Имена на variables"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:123
msgid "**Rules** (otherwise: syntax error):"
msgstr "**Правила** (иначе: синтактична грешка):"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:125
msgid "letters, digits, `_` and `$`; no spaces, no `-`;"
msgstr "букви, цифри, `_` и `$`; без интервали, без `-`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:126
msgid "must not start with a digit;"
msgstr "не може да започва с цифра;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:127
msgid "must not be a reserved word (`let`, `const`, `if`, `function`, `class`, ...);"
msgstr "не може да е запазена дума (`let`, `const`, `if`, `function`, `class`, ...);"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:128
msgid "names are **case-sensitive**: `model`, `MODEL` and `Model` are three variables."
msgstr "имената **различават малки и главни букви**: `model`, `MODEL` и `Model` са три различни variables."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:130
msgid "**Conventions** (good practice):"
msgstr "**Конвенции** (добра практика):"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:132
msgid "`camelCase` for variables: `serialNumber`, `firmwareLevel`, `isAffected`;"
msgstr "`camelCase` за variables: `serialNumber`, `firmwareLevel`, `isAffected`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:133
msgid "names that say what is inside: `firmwareLevel`, not `x` or `data2`;"
msgstr "имена, които казват какво има вътре: `firmwareLevel`, а не `x` или `data2`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:134
msgid "booleans start with `is`, `has`, `can`: `isEnabled`, `hasCert`;"
msgstr "имената на booleans започват с `is`, `has`, `can`: `isEnabled`, `hasCert`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:135
msgid "`UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for fixed settings: `const MIN_FIRMWARE_LEVEL = \"4.2.1.7\";`"
msgstr "`UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` за фиксирани настройки: `const MIN_FIRMWARE_LEVEL = \"4.2.1.7\";`"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:137
msgid "JSON keys vs variable names"
msgstr "Ключове в JSON срещу имена на variables"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:138
msgid "The keys in the report JSON use `snake_case` (`firmware_level`, `remote_login_enabled`). That is the data's naming - keep the keys as they are. Your own variables use `camelCase`: `const firmwareLevel = doc.inventory.details.firmware_level;`"
msgstr "Ключовете в JSON отчета са в `snake_case` (`firmware_level`, `remote_login_enabled`). Така са кръстени данните - оставете ключовете както са. Вашите собствени variables са в `camelCase`: `const firmwareLevel = doc.inventory.details.firmware_level;`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:143
msgid "**Check yourself:** which of these names are valid?"
msgstr "**Проверете се:** кои от тези имена са валидни?"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:147 site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:333
msgid "Answer"
msgstr "Отговор"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:148
msgid "Valid: `serial_number`, `$total`, `isRemote`, `MODEL`. Not valid: `2ndNode` (starts with a digit), `firmware-level` (`-` is minus), `const` (reserved word)."
msgstr "Валидни: `serial_number`, `$total`, `isRemote`, `MODEL`. Невалидни: `2ndNode` (започва с цифра), `firmware-level` (`-` е минус), `const` (запазена дума)."

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:153
msgid "3. Primitive types"
msgstr "3. Примитивни типове"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:155
msgid "A value in JavaScript is either a **primitive** (a single simple value) or an **object** (a structure with properties - like `doc`). The primitive types:"
msgstr "Една стойност в JavaScript е или **примитивна** (една проста стойност), или **обект** (структура с properties - като `doc`). Примитивните типове:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:158
msgid "Type"
msgstr "Тип"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:158
msgid "Examples"
msgstr "Примери"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:158
msgid "In the report data"
msgstr "В данните на отчета"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:160
msgid "counts, sizes (after conversion)"
msgstr "бройки, размери (след преобразуване)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:161
msgid "almost every value"
msgstr "почти всяка стойност"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:162
msgid "\"yes\" / \"no\" after conversion"
msgstr "\"yes\" / \"no\" след преобразуване"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:163
msgid "a key that is not in the document"
msgstr "ключ, който го няма в документа"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:164
msgid "\"no value\", written on purpose"
msgstr "\"няма стойност\", записано нарочно"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:166
msgid "(Two more, `bigint` and `symbol`, are rarely needed.)"
msgstr "(Има още два - `bigint` и `symbol`, но рядко трябват.)"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:179
msgid "Numbers"
msgstr "Numbers"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:181
msgid "Whole numbers and decimals are the same type, `number`:"
msgstr "Целите и дробните числа са от един и същ тип - `number`:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:193
msgid "Decimals are not exact"
msgstr "Дробните числа не са точни"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:194
msgid "`0.1 + 0.2` gives `0.30000000000000004`. Numbers are stored in binary, so most decimals are approximations. Round results before you show them."
msgstr "`0.1 + 0.2` дава `0.30000000000000004`. Числата се пазят в двоичен вид, затова повечето дробни числа са приближения. Закръглявайте резултатите, преди да ги покажете."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-variables-and-types.md:199
msgid "**Numbers in memory:** [1. Bits and integers](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}, [2. Fractions and 0.1](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}, [4. 0.1 + 0.2](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}, [6. NaN and Infinity](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Числата в паметта:** [1. Битове и цели числа](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}, [2. Дроби и 0.1](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}, [4. 0.1 + 0.2](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}, [6. NaN и Infinity](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
